  "details": "Looks like Simplified Chinese and Traditional Chinese are sharing the same language categories. It's correct, but it should not be displayed as \"简体中文\". should be display as the website did, remove the first half and keep the secound half: \"中文\". \n\nIn academic terms, Simplified Chinese and Traditional Chinese are just two different written habits of the Chinese language, as they should be called \"中文\"(Chinese), relative to other international languages.",
